// Arrows that go on up with `*` among them and along more than one tree,
// and a `for` that reacts to the sibling after
// (Inputs/tree_paths.ent).
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_paths.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

//   house(7) -- ground -- hall        house -Feeds-> fuse (60 watts)
//           |          `- den
//           `- upper(3) -- bed
// The parent, then from there the nearest with a colour: the floor's own
// is not asked, so the bed gets the house's, not `upper`'s.
// CHECK:      hall in ground, coloured 7
// CHECK-NEXT: den in ground, coloured 7
// CHECK-NEXT: bed in upper, coloured 7
// The nearest with a colour, and what that is in: only the bed has one
// that is in something.
// CHECK-NEXT: bed: 3 of upper in house
// Up one tree and on along another.
// CHECK-NEXT: upper in house on 60 watts
// CHECK-NEXT: ground in house on 60 watts
// The first time, every thing with a sibling after it: ground and hall.
// Then the den changes, which the hall is before.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: house 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: fuse 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: ground 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: upper 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: hall 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: den 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: bed 0
// Nothing changes: nothing runs.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: house 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: fuse 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: ground 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: upper 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: hall 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: den 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: bed 0
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
